<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guadix</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guadix is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the high plateau north of the Sierra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a>. Founded as the Roman colony of Acci, it became an early bishopric and, under Muslim rule, the town of Wadi Ash, briefly the seat of an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> after 1145. It belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Granada until it surrendered to the Catholic Monarchs in 1489, and is known for its cave dwellings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guadix.jpg" alt="Guadix" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: agracier - NO VIEWS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moorish_Castle_-_Cathedral_-_in_Guadix_Spain_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
